      },
      "geometry": "rect",
      "lineWidth": 0,
      "text": "Shabani et al. (2021) explained that inventory record inaccuracy occurs when the quantity recorded in the inventory system does not match the quantity physically available. In practical SME operations, this mismatch can result from delayed stock encoding, manual stock counts, and branch-level recording inconsistencies, which contribute to stock discrepancies, stockout risks, and unreliable inventory information for day-to-day decisions.",
